      "headline": "The March of the Umbers",
      "text": "The dust rose in thick, choking clouds as the great host of the North began its trek. Lord Jon Umber sat high in his saddle, a mountain of a man amidst the sea of steel and boiled leather. Behind him, the weight of the North moved in a long, grinding line: the Glovers, the Norreys, the Liddles, and the Boltons. Roose Bolton rode in the shadow of the Umber banners, his pale eyes as cold as a winter storm. He spoke to no one, his face a mask of stillness as the dry summer air bit at his cheeks. The column stretched toward the south, a slow, heavy river of men leaving the warmth of Winterfell behind.",
      "pov": "Jon Umber"
    },
    {
      "fact": 2,
      "headline": "Departure for the Wall",
      "text": "The air was crisp, carrying the scent of pine and dying summer. Jon Snow checked the cinch on his saddle one last time, feeling the reassuring weight of Benjen’s letter tucked deep in his bag. Six men of the household moved quietly around him, checking their gear in the pale morning light. A white shape flickered at the edge of the tree line—Ghost, moving like a ghost through the undergrowth, his eyes fixed on the path ahead. With a heavy heart and a steady hand, Jon turned his horse north, leaving the warmth of the castle for the long road to Castle Black.",
      "pov": "Jon Snow"
    },
    {
      "fact": 3,
      "headline": "Silence at the Moat",
      "text": "The three great towers of Moat Cailin loomed like broken teeth against the darkening sky. On the battlements, the rhythmic twang of bowstrings punctuated the silence as archers took their stations, watching the empty road. Below, the causeway had been cleared of the rubble and fallen stone, leaving a path that led straight into the heart of the swamp. Robb Stark stood amidst the stillness, his youth betrayed only by the smoothness of his face, though his eyes were old. He looked south, waiting for a messenger, a bird, or a sign, but there was nothing but the wind whistling through the ruins.",
      "pov": "Robb Stark"
    }
  ]
